---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DOCUMENTS, CARDS, COLOPHON, readingMinutes } from '../../data/participate';

const byline: Record<string, string> = {
  'six-months-of-a-library': 'Report',
  'the-next-three-years': 'Plan',
  'a-record-with-a-keeper': 'The case for support',
  'ways-to-help': 'Invitation',
  'how-a-collection-comes-in': 'An account of one accession',
  'six-months-of-a-library-the-timeline': 'Handout',
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Participate · America's School Trust Library"
  description="The Library's September 2026 shelf: a six-month report, a three-year plan, the case for support, the invitations, an account of one collection arriving, and a one-page timeline. Each in web text and as a PDF."
  sourceId="participate-index"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    <p class="kicker">Participate</p>
    <h1>Participate</h1>

    <p>
      In 1785, two years before the Constitutional Convention, Congress decided
      that one square mile in every township of the western surveys would
      belong to the schools &mdash; a township being the six-mile survey square
      the country was laid out in. Not to a church, not to a governor: to the
      children who would live there.
    </p>

    <p>
      These are the Library&rsquo;s own documents about that work and about
      itself: what it did in its first six months, what it plans to do next,
      the case it makes for being kept, the ways in for five kinds of reader,
      and one account of a collection arriving. Each is on this site as web
      text and as a PDF you can print. The Library is not asking you for money.
      It asks for documents and hands.
    </p>
  </article>

  <section class="doc-list not-prose">
    {DOCUMENTS.map((doc) => (
      <article class="doc-card">
        <p class="doc-kind">{byline[doc.slug]}</p>
        <h2 class="doc-title">
          <a href={`/participate/${doc.slug}/`}>{doc.title}</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="doc-blurb">{doc.blurb}</p>
        <p class="doc-links">
          <a href={`/participate/${doc.slug}/`}>Read on this site</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href={`/participate/${doc.slug}.pdf`}>web PDF</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href={`/participate/${doc.slug}-press.pdf`}>press PDF</a>
          <span class="doc-stat">
            {doc.pages} pages &middot; about {readingMinutes(doc.pages)} minutes
          </span>
        </p>
        {doc.slug === 'ways-to-help' && (
          <div class="doc-children">
            <p class="doc-children-label">
              Five cards travel with it, one for each way in. Each is four
              pages and stands on its own:
            </p>
            <ul>
              {CARDS.map((card) => (
                <li>
                  <a href={`/participate/${card.slug}/`}>{card.title}</a>
                  &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;<span class="card-blurb">{card.blurb}</span>
                  &nbsp;(<a href={`/participate/${card.slug}.pdf`}>web PDF</a>
                  &nbsp;·&nbsp;
                  <a href={`/participate/${card.slug}-press.pdf`}>press PDF</a>)
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        )}
      </article>
    ))}
  </section>

  <article class="prose prose-slate mt-10 max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    <h2>A note on the two PDFs</h2>
    <p>
      The web copy is the one to read on a screen or print at home. The press
      copy is print-ready, with bleed and crop marks, and is the file to hand a
      printer; it is larger and will look wrong on screen, because the page is
      bigger than the paper by the width of the trim.
    </p>

    <h2>How to say yes</h2>
    <p>
      Write to the Library at
      <a href="mailto:library@schooltrusts.net">library@schooltrusts.net</a>,
      addressed to the Secretary, Kenneth Magee. Say what you have done that
      bears on this and what you would take on. The lighter ways in &mdash; a
      source, a correction, a state to watch &mdash; are on the
      <a href="/contribute/">Contribute</a> page.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Library has not yet filed its application for federal tax-exempt
      recognition; it is being prepared. No federal tax-exemption determination
      has been issued, and until one is, the Library does not describe
      contributions as tax-deductible.
    </p>
    <p class="colophon-note">{COLOPHON}</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #a88a4e;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .doc-list {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }
  .doc-card {
    background: var(--linen-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-border);
    border-left: 4px solid #c9a24a;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem 1.1rem;
  }
  .doc-kind {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #8a7340;
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
  }
  .doc-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
  }
  .doc-title a {
    color: var(--trust-blue);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .doc-title a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .doc-blurb {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.99rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .doc-links {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: #4e617c;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .doc-links a {
    color: #1d4ed8;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .doc-stat {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    color: #6b7a8d;
  }
  .doc-children {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-border);
  }
  .doc-children-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: #4e617c;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .doc-children ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    list-style: disc;
  }
  .doc-children li {
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }
  .doc-children a {
    color: #1d4ed8;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .card-blurb {
    color: #4a5568;
  }
  .colophon-note {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: #6b7a8d;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-border);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
